Here's a work-around for known (VMS-specific) problem:

     If you want to use the number_pad option for input on a vt100/200/&c
style terminal, you'll have to patch the vt100 termcap entry.  The current
value for initialization string is
        :ti=4\E<\E(B\E)0:
which sets the terminal mode into a known state.  However, some other
code (deep in the bowels of the SMG library) also turns on "application
keypad mode", which makes the vt100/&c keypad send escape sequences
instead of numbers.  NetHack's number_pad mode currently requires actual
numbers.  Insert the escape sequence for "numeric keypad mode" into the
initialization string:
        :ti=4\E<\E(B\E)0\E>:
                        ^^^  insert 3 characters, "\E>", before colon
This may be fixed in the code someday, since it doesn't belong in this
termcap entry.  (NetHack doesn't use the 'ke' entry at present, which is
where this _does_ belong and where is happens to be already.)

